Description: Pair close tags by a name key that ignores whitespace
 A close tag closed the current element only when its name was
 byte-identical, so "</{{element}}>" did not close "<{{ element }}>". The
 close tag token now carries its parts when the name holds a template, and
 names are compared by a key with whitespace and a trailing "/" removed
 and letters lower-cased, as a browser ignores "/" in "</div/>".
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/parse-for-eslint.test.ts ("Twig as part of the markup structure")
Last-Update: 2026-10-14
